    {
      "fileName": "crude-communication.json",
      "id": "sbYDDDUWYN6Qx71k",
      "name": "Crude Communication",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "sbYDDDUWYN6Qx71k",
        "folder": "7HTBHy5tJLbxzEI8",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Crude Communication",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Even if you don't speak a creature's language, you can rely on inflection, root words, and body language to infer rudimentary meaning.</p>\n<p>If you interact with a creature for at least 10 minutes and that creature can speak a language, the GM rolls a secret Society check with a DC appropriate for the language's rarity.</p>\n<p>On a success, you understand the gist of the meaning and can communicate basic concepts back to the creature; on a failure, you are mistaken or communicate incorrect concepts.</p>\n<p>If you're legendary in Society, you can communicate instantly without needing to attempt a Society check; even if you didn't know the medium of communication the creature uses (speech, sign language, and so on), you intuit this information as soon as they try to communicate.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Linguist Dedication"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Player Core 2"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "archetype"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
      "category": "class"
    },
